We are currently working on a senior design project at Drexel University.
Our project idea is a system that will:

   - Gather and present real-time infrastructure power usage


   - Prioritize power distribution for processes and devices
      - For peak summer power usage turn off noncritical processes and
      devices.

We are curious to know if anyone in the community is already working on a
similar project and if so can they offer guidance.

In particular we would like information on where in the Linux power
management stack we should place either of these features.
This email is not subscribed to the list so please reply to all.

Thanks,
Marisol Saldana
Renee von Mechow
Bryan Quigley

